The value is 25~\% above its limit.
% a comment with \% in it
a \\% a comment after a line break
50\\\% is not a comment

----------------------------------------------------

[
	"The value is 25~",
	["function", "\\%"],
	" above its limit.\r\n",

	["comment", "% a comment with \\% in it"],

	"\r\na ",
	["function", "\\\\"],
	["comment", "% a comment after a line break"],

	"\r\n50",
	["function", "\\\\"],
	["function", "\\%"],
	" is not a comment"
]

----------------------------------------------------

Checks that an escaped percent sign is not a comment, while a percent sign after an escaped backslash is.

See https://github.com/PrismJS/prism/issues/3563
